[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Test preparations

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-003-MILUAV
TITLE: Test Environment
STATEMENT: Testing shall be conducted in a controlled environment with hardware-in-the-loop simulation, flight test facilities, and security testing laboratories.
RATIONALE: Proper test environment ensures valid test results.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-004-MILUAV
TITLE: Test Tools
STATEMENT: Testing shall use automated test tools, static analysis tools, security testing tools, and real-time analysis tools approved for military software testing.
RATIONALE: Appropriate test tools ensure comprehensive testing coverage.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Test descriptions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-005-MILUAV
TITLE: Unit Testing
STATEMENT: All software components shall undergo unit testing with 100% code coverage, including boundary conditions, error handling, and performance requirements.
RATIONALE: Unit testing ensures individual component reliability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-006-MILUAV
TITLE: Integration Testing
STATEMENT: Component integration testing shall verify interface compatibility, data flow, and system behavior under normal and fault conditions.
RATIONALE: Integration testing ensures system interoperability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-007-MILUAV
TITLE: System Testing
STATEMENT: System testing shall validate end-to-end functionality, performance requirements, security requirements, and safety requirements in operational scenarios.
RATIONALE: System testing validates complete system operation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-008-MILUAV
TITLE: Flight Testing
STATEMENT: Flight testing shall be conducted in controlled environments to validate autonomous flight, mission execution, and emergency procedures.
RATIONALE: Flight testing validates real-world operational capabilities.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-009-MILUAV
TITLE: Security Testing
STATEMENT: Security testing shall include penetration testing, vulnerability assessment, and cryptographic validation per military security standards.
RATIONALE: Security testing ensures protection against threats.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Requirements traceability

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-010-MILUAV
TITLE: Test Traceability
STATEMENT: All test cases shall be traceable to software requirements with bidirectional traceability maintained throughout the testing process.
RATIONALE: Test traceability ensures complete requirements validation.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Notes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-011-MILUAV
TITLE: Test Documentation
STATEMENT: All test results shall be documented with detailed reports, including test procedures, results, issues, and recommendations for military compliance.
RATIONALE: Test documentation ensures auditability and compliance.

[[/SECTION]] 